# The decoder's entry point.
#
# Protocol: stdin gives two lines, the input path and the output path
# (natively `/file/<absolute path>`). stdout gets `FRAME width height ncomp
# kind`, then either `DECODED`, with the P5 or P6 image written to the output
# path, or, for input M2 does not decode yet, `NOT_YET <reason>` (progressive,
# arithmetic, 12-bit, 4-component or multi-scan) with no output file; the
# exit status is 0. A refusal is a trap `REFUSED CODE: message` on stderr
# with exit status 1; any other trap is a decoder bug. The output is opened
# before decoding, so a refusal mid-scan can leave a partial file: the
# harness ignores it, and the service deletes the request directory.

: main ( -- )
  read-line drop :> inp
  read-line drop :> outp
  inp source.load markers.open :> j
  j markers.walk
  j huffman.scan-tables :> tabs
  j markers.frame-line println
  j rows.unsupported :> why
  why str.len
  [ "NOT_YET " why str.concat println ]
  [
    j tabs rows.setup :> d
    outp d decoder.width d decoder.height d decoder.ncomp ppm.open :> h
    d [ ( bytes -- ) h swap ppm.row ] rows.decode
    h host.close drop
    "DECODED" println
  ]
  if ;
